ivities and instilling dread. As midnight strikes, a mysterious figure dressed as the Red Death, covered in blood and wearing a corpse-like mask, enters the ball, paralyzing the guests with terror; Prince Prospero, enraged, pursues the figure through all seven rooms with a dagger, only to collapse dead upon confronting it in the black chamber, revealing the figure to be an empty shell, as the plague claims every reveller and extinguishes all light and life.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"characters\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\",\n      \"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n      \"aliases\": [\n        \"Prospero\",\n        \"the mummer\"\n      ],\n      \"role\": null,\n      \"appearance\": null,\n      \"personality\": null,\n      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n      \"descriptions\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Prince Prospero is a self-indulgent and authoritarian figure who isolates himself and a thousand courtiers in a fortified abbey to escape the Red Death, demonstrating a profound disregard for the suffering beyond his walls. His actions shift from arrogant detachment to frenzied rage when confronted by a figure embodying the plague he sought to evade, culminating in his violent pursuit and immediate death, revealing his hubris and inability to face mortality.\",\n          \"source_position\": 1894,\n          \"chapter_index\": null,\n          \"confidence\": \"llm_refined\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relationships\": {},\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"Prince Prospero isolates himself and a thousand courtiers in a fortified abbey to escape the Red Death\",\n          \"quote\": \"Prince Prospero seals himself and a thousand courtiers within a fortified, elaborately designed abbey to escape contagion.\",\n          \"position\": \"Chapter 1\",\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He hosts a lavish, indulgent masquerade while the plague rages outside\",\n          \"quote\": \"It was toward the close of the fifth or sixth month of his seclusion, and while the pestilence raged most furiously abroad, that the Prince Prospero entertained his thousand friends at a masked ball of the most unusual magnificence.\",\n          \"position\": \"Chapter 1, Position 1894\",\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He is enraged by the figure dressed as the Red Death and demands it be hanged\",\n          \"quote\": \"Insult us with this blasphemous mockery? Seize him and unmask him -- that we may know whom we have to hang at sunrise, from the battlements!\",\n          \"position\": \"Chapter 1, Position 11148\",\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He pursues the figure through all seven rooms in a fit of rage\",\n          \"quote\": \"It was then, however, that the Prince Prospero, maddening with rage and the shame of his own momentary cowardice, rushed hurriedly through the six chambers, while none followed him on account of a deadly terror that had...\",\n          \"position\": \"Chapter 1, Position 12389\",\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He collapses dead upon confronting the figure in the black chamber\",\n          \"quote\": \"There was a sharp cry -- and the dagger dropped gleaming upon the sable carpet, upon which, instantly afterwards, fell prostrate in death the Prince Prospero.\",\n          \"position\": \"Chapter 1, Position 12980\",\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"voice_notes\": null,\n      \"first_appearance_chapter\": 1,\n      \"mention_count\": 7,\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"is_narrator\": false,\n      \"narrative_role\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"pronunciations\": [\n    {\n      \"word\": \"Prospero\",\n      \"flag_reason\": \"proper_noun\",\n      \"occurrences\": 18,\n      \"first_posi