gin-top: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--accent-soft);\">Chapters</h3>\n            \n            <div class=\"chapter-card\">\n                <h4>\n                    <span>Chapter 1</span>\n                    <span class=\"meta\">2,443 words &middot; 16m</span>\n                </h4>\n                \n                <div class=\"chapter-summary\">The chapter opens with the devastating spread of the 'Red Death,' a gruesome plague marked by bleeding pores and rapid death, prompting Prince Prospero to seal himself and a thousand courtiers within a fortified, elaborately designed abbey to escape contagion. Inside, seven uniquely colored rooms—each with stained-glass windows matching their decor—host a lavish masked ball, illuminated only by firelight from external tripods, with the final black chamber featuring blood-red windows and a massive ebony clock that chimes hourly, halting the festivities and instilling dread. As midnight strikes, a mysterious figure dressed as the Red Death, covered in blood and wearing a corpse-like mask, enters the ball, paralyzing the guests with terror; Prince Prospero, enraged, pursues the figure through all seven rooms with a dagger, only to collapse dead upon confronting it in the black chamber, revealing the figure to be an empty shell, as the plague claims every reveller and extinguishes all light and life.</div>\n                \n                \n                <div class=\"chapter-characters\" style=\"margin-top: 0.75rem;\">\n                    <strong style=\"margin-right: 0.5rem; color: var(--muted);\">Characters:</strong>\n                    \n                    <span class=\"tag\">Prince Prospero</span>\n                    \n                    <span class=\"tag\">The masked figure (Red Death)</span>\n                    \n                    \n                </div>\n                \n            </div>\n            \n        </section>\n        </div>\n\n        <div id=\"characters\" class=\"tab-conten