{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_017kQdVwpZfZH9nYfsCgm9WX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Evaluation Complete\n\n**The Masque of the Red Death - Attempt 13 - FAIL (6.85/10)**\n\n### Summary\n\n| Category | Score | Notes |\n|----------|-------|-------|\n| Structure Detection | 10/10 | Correct - single chapter story |\n| Character Extraction | 3/10 | **CRITICAL FAILURE** - Antagonist merged with protagonist |\n| Character Profiles | 6/10 | Good for Prospero, missing antagonist |\n| Chapter Summaries | 9/10 | Excellent - correctly identifies both characters |\n| Pronunciation Guide | 6/10 | Too many false positives |\n| HTML Presentation | 8/10 | Clean, functional |\n| **Overall** | **6.85/10** | Threshold: 8.0 |\n\n### Critical Issue (13 attempts, still unresolved)\n\n\"The mummer\" (the Red Death personification) is incorrectly listed as an **alias** of Prince Prospero. They are different characters - Prince Prospero **dies** after confronting the mummer.\n\n### Key Finding from Attempt 13\n\nThe `_entities_in_death_relationship()` function is **never called**, proving the merge happens **before** cross-group resolution. The fix must target an earlier stage:\n\n1. **Pairwise alias resolution** (`_llm_alias_resolution()` or `_heuristic_alias_resolution()`)\n2. **Name classification** (`_is_descriptive_handle()`) - \"the mummer\" may be misclassified as a proper name instead of an epithet\n3. **Initial extraction** - proposers may already be associating them\n\n### Recommended Next Approach (Attempt 14)\n\n1. **Add debug logging** to trace exactly where the merge happens\n2. **Post-processing split** - Use summary output (which correctly identifies both characters) to validate/correct character extraction\n3. **Classification fix** - Make `_is_descriptive_handle()` more conservative about \"the X\" patterns\n\nThe evaluation loop will restart with `PROMPT_fix.md` to address these issues."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":399,"cache_read_input_tokens":84405,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":399,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dc8ad2b7-7600-4f50-8c29-521c9050bc3c","uuid":"ae6ac0c4-7db0-4169-ac4c-a37df58bbd7a"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":165425,"duration_api_ms":165816,"num_turns":17,"result":"## Evaluation Complete\n\n**The Masque of the Red Death - Attempt 13 - FAIL (6.85/10)**\n\n### Summary\n\n| Category | Score | Notes |\n|----------|-------|-------|\n| Structure Detection | 10/10 | Correct - single chapter story |\n| Character Extraction | 3/10 | **CRITICAL FAILURE** - Antagonist merged with protagonist |\n| Character Profiles | 6/10 | Good for Prospero, missing antagonist |\n| Chapter Summaries | 9/10 | Excellent - correctly identifies both characters |\n| Pronunciation Guide | 6/10 | Too many false positives |\n| HTML Presentation | 8/10 | Clean, functional |\n| **Overall** | **6.85/10** | Threshold: 8.0 |\n\n### Critical Issue (13 attempts, still unresolved)\n\n\"The mummer\" (the Red Death personification) is incorrectly listed as an **alias** of Prince Prospero. They are different characters - Prince Prospero **dies** after confronting the mummer.\n\n### Key Finding from Attempt 13\n\nThe `_entities_in_death_relationship()` function is **never called**, proving the merge happens **before** cross-group resolution. The fix must target an earlier stage:\n\n1. **Pairwise alias resolution** (`_llm_alias_resolution()` or `_heuristic_alias_resolution()`)\n2. **Name classification** (`_is_descriptive_handle()`) - \"the mummer\" may be misclassified as a proper name instead of an epithet\n3. **Initial extraction** - proposers may already be associating them\n\n### Recommended Next Approach (Attempt 14)\n\n1. **Add debug logging** to trace exactly where the merge happens\n2. **Post-processing split** - Use summary output (which correctly identifies both characters) to validate/correct character extraction\n3. **Classification fix** - Make `_is_descriptive_handle()` more conservative about \"the X\" patterns\n\nThe evaluation loop will restart with `PROMPT_fix.md` to address these issues.","session_id":"dc8ad2b7-7600-4f50-8c29-521c9